WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.429 --> 00:00:10.649
<v><b>Ned:</b></v> Hi, I’m Ned. Welcome to Portchester Castle.

2
00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:22.800
Portchester Castle is over one thousand seven hundred years old.

3
00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:27.558
It’s near Portsmouth, a city on the south coast of England.

4
00:00:30.107 --> 00:00:32.925
The castle is part of English Heritage.

5
00:00:33.081 --> 00:00:40.190
English Heritage is a charity, which manages over four hundred old buildings and monuments in England.

6
00:00:41.351 --> 00:00:46.931
With so many old buildings, there are also lots of reports of ghosts.

7
00:00:47.526 --> 00:00:52.397
And ghosts are sometimes a problem for staff and visitors at English Heritage.

8
00:00:52.963 --> 00:00:58.543
In fact, some staff decided to leave their jobs because of the ghosts.

9
00:01:00.922 --> 00:01:07.918
I’ve come here to Portchester to find out more about reports of not one, but four ghosts!

10
00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:12.747
And many of the ghosts come from different times in Portchester’s long history.

11
00:01:20.026 --> 00:01:23.085
Portchester Castle dates back to Roman Britain;

12
00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:28.424
the Romans built the original castle here in the year two hundred and ninety.

13
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.946
The first ghost report also comes from Roman times.

14
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.838
Visitors report that they see the ghost of a Roman soldier guarding the walls,

15
00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:43.151
but they say they don’t feel frightened.

16
00:01:47.598 --> 00:01:53.404
In the Middle Ages, Portchester became a favourite castle for the kings and queens of England.

17
00:01:54.480 --> 00:02:05.725
During this time, a small monastery was built. There’s a church here now in place of the monastery.

18
00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:13.570
People say that they see a man dressed in black here and they think he is the ghost of a monk from the monastery.

19
00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:21.019
Surprisingly, people don’t feel frightened when they see him. They say that he disappears when they look at him.

20
00:02:24.219 --> 00:02:32.036
Our first two ghosts are not very frightening, but the next ghost really frightens people – the White Lady.

21
00:02:43.281 --> 00:02:47.444
Some people believe that this is the ghost of Charlotte White.

22
00:02:47.897 --> 00:02:52.146
She was a woman who visited the castle in the nineteenth century.

23
00:02:52.627 --> 00:03:01.067
Charlotte’s baby fell into the water and poor Charlotte also died when she tried to save her child.

24
00:03:03.163 --> 00:03:07.525
The most frightening ghost of all is a man on a black horse.

25
00:03:07.865 --> 00:03:15.229
Both castle visitors and staff say that they see him. One of the staff who saw the ghost said,

26
00:03:16.036 --> 00:03:18.302
‘It got bigger and bigger.

27
00:03:18.415 --> 00:03:22.295
It started to come towards me and I screamed and ran away’.

28
00:03:22.791 --> 00:03:31.146
People also say they hear the sound of horses; one visitor even heard the sound of horses on a video he filmed.

29
00:03:32.874 --> 00:03:38.425
One of the strange things about the man on the horse is that we don’t know who he is

30
00:03:38.538 --> 00:03:42.475
or which part of Portchester’s long history he is from.

31
00:03:48.055 --> 00:03:57.429
I was quite sure I didn’t believe in ghosts before I came here, but, after a day at Portchester, I’m not so sure.